  "data": {
    "id": 825305,
    "name": "Matsutake mushrooms",
    "description": "<p>Matsutake or Pine Mushroom</p>\n<p>Tricholoma murrillianum</p><br />\n<p>Foraged weekly less than a mile from the Pacific Ocean, these matsutakes are choice mushrooms, desired for their spicy odor and flavor, and meaty texture. Excellent in rice as in the classic dish Matsutake Gohan; some simply grill them and others love them caramelized over vanilla ice cream.</p><br />\n<p>I get as much sand off of the base of matsutakes, but I don't trim the bottom because matsutakes grow in sandy soil and I like to leave that identifying feature in tact for confidence in consuming. Trim bottoms off before cooking.&nbsp;</p>",
